                <pb facs="0615" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg481"/>

                <head>No. 333.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Anderson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 7,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anderson</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, Copenhagen:</hi></p>
                <p>Benson extradition papers mailed yesterday. Is Benson’s identity established to
                    satisfaction of Danish Government, and would prisoner be delivered to United
                    States officer now on his way from California, if send to Denmark?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
